WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(tense staccato music)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.390
- I was having a lot of
fatigue and body aches.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.850
I just thought it was
exhaustion from traveling.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:06.990
But the next morning

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.170
I woke up with rashes all over my hands.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:11.910
The lesions started spreading

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:15.480
to the more usual suspect areas,

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.390
so that really made the
doctors sort of confirm

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.213
that what I had was monkeypox.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.660
- [Narrator] Kevin Kwong
believes he was first infected

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.290
in late June, about a
month after monkeypox cases

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.690
began to be reported in the U.S.

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.970
- It was sort of this,
like, mystery disease.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.310
I think I approached things cautiously,

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:36.180
but at the same time,

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.640
I wasn't even sure what to be aware of.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.010
- [Narrator] By late July,
the World Health Organization

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.650
declared it a global health emergency,

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.510
their highest level of alert.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.390
- It will not be the
next COVID-19 pandemic,

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.040
but as a public health professional,

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.290
I am very worried about what's unfolding,

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.970
because this has the possibility

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:57.180
to become a new virus
that circulates regularly.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.640
- [Narrator] So how does monkeypox spread

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.373
and what can be done to
contain this outbreak?

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.310
It's called monkeypox

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:08.250
because it was first
detected in research monkeys

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:11.580
and because it's closely
related to smallpox.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.110
- The way I think about smallpox,

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.260
it's the human version of monkeypox.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.740
It's not engineered to exploit
human cells and human bodies.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.050
We're like an accidental host.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.510
- [Narrator] Monkeypox is
endemic to parts of Africa

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:27.000
where it mostly circulates among rodents.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.010
Occasionally, from close interactions,

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.300
like hunting or eating,

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.660
monkeypox will spread
from an animal to a human,

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.510
and in May of 2022,
someone showing symptoms

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.390
traveled from Nigeria
to the United Kingdom.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.780
Soon after, other cases
began appearing in the U.K.,

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.630
then Portugal, Sweden, the U.S.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:48.150
- Previously the outbreaks
were fairly limited.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.990
Epidemiologists were able
to bring it under control.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:51.900
In the current outbreak,

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.060
it's spreading fairly
efficiently between humans,

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.070
primarily through sexual contact.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:56.903
- [Narrator] When infected,

00:01:56.903 --> 00:01:58.800
monkeypox gets into your bloodstream

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.990
and creates lesions on the skin.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.420
While it can spread through
respiratory droplets

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.950
or bodily fluids, with this
2022 outbreak, it's rare.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:09.420
The most common way it spreads

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.450
is through skin-to-skin
contact with those lesions.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:15.570
- We know that during
intimate contact or cuddling,

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.810
et cetera, you make these
micro-abrasions in the skin.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:22.200
You can't really see it a lot
of times, but they're there.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.500
So the virus just jumps
from the person who has it,

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:30.090
and there's tons of it, into
one of these micro-abrasions.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.040
- [Narrator] Once infected,
it can take a while

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.630
for symptoms to appear.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.180
That can happen as soon as
five days after infection

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.430
to nearly three weeks after,

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.980
but they usually appear around here,

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.900
and these first few days of symptoms

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.110
look like a typical illness
as your immune system kicks in

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:47.880
to begin fighting the disease:

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.740
fever, headache, fatigue,

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.410
and even the swelling of your lymph nodes.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:55.770
It's after that, that the rash
and lesions typically begin,

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:58.380
especially on the hands and face.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.080
With the outbreak that began in 2022,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.150
the lesions appeared differently.

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:05.310
They can be localized more on the genitals

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:07.500
and even appear more like bumps,

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.600
something that not all
medical professionals

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.220
are trained to identify.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.080
- [Kevin] Even when I
went into Urgent Care,

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:16.470
they told me that this was
definitely not monkeypox,

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:19.140
because the way that
monkeypox had been appearing

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:20.550
in photos that they've received,

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.400
were larger lesions, umbilicated,

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.310
so kind of like donut-shaped,
all throughout the body,

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:29.370
and I just didn't have
any of that at the time.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.440
- People thought to have visible rashes,

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.850
like what you'd see in the textbooks,

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.730
were these huge boils on people's arms,

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.560
but they could be very, very subtle.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.720
- [Narrator] Dr. Chin-Hong
was able to diagnose

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.820
and prescribe Kevin TPOXX,

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.410
an antiviral medication

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.960
that the government
already had stockpiled.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.520
- [Caitlin] There was
a lot of preparedness,

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.070
particularly after the
September 11th attacks

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:51.600
and the anthrax mailings,

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.730
that went into preparing for smallpox.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.070
We had a lot of tools
already in the arsenal

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:59.400
to fight smallpox but that
also worked for monkeypox.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.310
- [Narrator] The stockpile
includes an approved vaccine.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:05.010
U.S. authorities are
testing already-made doses

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.860
and ordering 2.5 million more.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:10.380
- And so we are in a
relatively good position

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:13.170
against this virus than we
would be against a virus

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:16.620
that we had never prepared for before,

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:17.460
but we need to make sure

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.370
that we use those tools
appropriately and aggressively

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:22.800
in order to bring this
virus under control.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.390
- [Narrator] The vaccine can also be used

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.740
as part of the treatment.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.410
If given within four
days after the exposure,

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.940
it can prevent the infection

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:31.860
or at least make it less severe.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.900
- You can develop your antibodies,

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.880
because it's, like, so slow,

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.370
because it's trying to find
a rat and it's a human.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:39.960
- [Narrator] The vaccines
to come available

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.670
have been restricted to the community

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:45.210
monkeypox is affecting most:
men who have sex with men.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:46.770
- Among the 6,000 cases

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.230
currently reported to the
World Health Organization,

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.870
98% are in men who have sex with men,

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:53.430
but we also want to be very careful

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.580
not to stigmatize the disease
or to give the impression

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.130
that it is exclusively and forever limited

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.500
to men who have sex with men,
because that's not the case.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.100
- It's a human virus.
It can attack anyone.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.120
- [Narrator] Public health officials

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:07.980
are concerned about the virus spreading

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:09.480
to other vulnerable groups,

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:12.570
like children or even U.S. animals,

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:14.580
which is why the messaging is the same

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.327
as the last outbreak we saw:

00:05:16.327 --> 00:05:19.163
"Stop the spread and get vaccinated."

00:05:19.163 --> 00:05:22.413
(tense staccato music)

